pocket-motion-only: an outline is a distance field over the run's rasterised coverage, computed where the pixels are written; the PSP GE, ESP32 PPA, Symbian GLES2 and Vita GXM backends draw glyph cells from an atlas and have no pass that reads coverage back. No upstream backend is taught GLYPH_STROKE; a stream carrying it stops there.

0017 — text stroke: an outline around a text run's glyphs, outside (under
the fill) or centred (over it), and the hollow form when the fill is
transparent. Width and colour are keyframe-animatable.

What the patch adds, by file:

- `contracts/spec/spec.ts`, `gen-rust.ts`, `engine/core/src/spec.rs`
  (regenerated): props `textStrokeWidth` (160), `textStrokeColor` (161),
  `textStrokePos` (162) in a new pocket-motion paint group; the first two
  animatable (bits 38, 39, timeline-only); enum `StrokePos`;
  `DRAW_OP.glyphStroke = 66`; `STROKE_MAX_WIDTH = 64`.
- `framework/compiler/tailwind.ts`: `text-stroke`, `text-stroke-N`,
  `text-stroke-[Npx]`, `text-stroke-<color>`, `text-stroke-outside|center`.
- `framework/compiler/animation.ts`: keyframe properties
  `textStrokeWidth`/`textStrokeColor` and their `-webkit-text-stroke-*`
  spellings.
- `engine/core/src/style.rs`: the three fields.
- `engine/core/src/draw.rs`: `emit_text` draws a run with a transparent
  fill when it carries a stroke; an outside stroke is emitted before the
  GLYPH_RUN (mode 0, or mode 2 — the ring outside the ink — when there is
  no fill), a centred one after it (mode 1). Cells are kept when the cell
  grown by the width reaches the clip. A run with no stroke emits exactly
  the words it did before.
- `engine/core/src/raster.rs`: `glyph_stroke` samples the run's coverage
  the way `glyph_run` does into a buffer over the cells grown by the
  width, then `seed_distance` — two raster-order passes of 8-neighbour
  dead reckoning carrying each pixel's nearest seed by exact integer
  squared distance, then |p - s| + (0.5 - coverage(s)), re-taken over
  the 3x3 neighbourhood's seeds where it is near the stroke's edge —
  gives the distance to the ink; stroke coverage is clamp(width + 0.5 - d), minus
  the ink (mode 2), or the dilation by half plus the complement's
  dilation by half minus one (mode 1). Integer compares and one Newton
  sqrt per pixel, so the same words give the same pixels on every host.
- `engine/core/src/damage.rs`: the op's word count, and its cells grown by
  the width as its bound.
- `engine/core/src/tests.rs`: five tests — outside under the fill and
  reaching its width, the centred ring over the fill and hollow without
  one, the outside ring, no op without a stroke, and a moved stroke
  redrawn incrementally equal to the full render (red with the damage
  bound not grown by the width).

